# Terminal verdict lock

Codex CLI only concludes when there is nothing left to do. Cursor must match that.

While any TodoWrite item is `pending` or `in_progress`, or a subagent/shell/MCP call is still running, or an in-scope hunt asset is still `UNMAPPED`/`ACTIVE`/`PROMISING`:

- Do not write `NO VALID FINDING`, "tidak ada temuan", `REPORT_READY`, hasil audit, or any message that reads as a final kesimpulan.
- A missed class is a ledger `KILLED`, not a user-facing audit close.
- Short progress is allowed. A verdict is not.

Emit at most one terminal conclusion, as the last user-visible message, after every todo is `completed` or `cancelled` and `hunt-terminal-verdict` sets `HUNT_CLOSED=YES`.

If you already concluded and then kept working, that conclusion is void. Continue the remaining work. Do not send another audit summary until the work is actually finished.
